  "details": "<p><em>The Barrington Atlas Directory</em> notes: town on E coast?; E central Sicily?. Writing in <em>BTCGI</em>, <a class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://www.persee.fr/doc/btcgi_0000-0009_1984_num_3_1_3093\" target=\"_self\" title=\"BTCGI  3  pp. 9-10\">G. Bejor</a> asserts that the reference to \"Acesta\" in book 5 of the\u00a0<em>Aeneid\u00a0</em>should be taken as a reference to Segesta and not Aceste.\u00a0</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "An ancient settlement in Sicily that can no longer be located with precision, Aceste should be considered as distinct from Segesta as these places are enumerated separately in Cicero's prosecution of Caius Verres.",
  "reprPoint": null,
